  "description": "The lawful use of the property is as a public house (Use Class Sui Generis), comprising a ground floor drinking establishment, basement storage, and ancillary first-floor kitchen and office accommodation. The proposed development seeks to retain the public house use at ground floor and basement level, whilst introducing residential accommodation at upper levels, which constitutes a material change of use from Sui Generis to Use Class C3 (dwellinghouses). In particular, the first floor will be converted from ancillary pub use (kitchen and office) into 2 self-contained residential units (1 x 1-bedroom and 1 x 2-bedroom flat), together with a communal roof terrace to the rear, representing a clear change of use from ancillary commercial floorspace to residential.\n\nThe proposal also includes a three-storey upward extension, forming new second, third and fourth floors, all of which will be in residential use (Use Class C3). The second floor will comprise 1 x 1-bedroom and 1 x 2-bedroom flat, the third floor will comprise 2 x 1-bedroom flats, and the fourth floor will comprise a further 2 x 1-bedroom flats, thereby intensifying the residential use of the site. Access arrangements will be clearly defined, with the primary entrance to the residential units provided at ground floor level from Lilian Road, connecting into a dedicated residential circulation core addressing the main street frontage, whilst the public house will retain its principal access from Greyhound Terrace, ensuring a clear separation of uses.\n\nAt roof level, the development incorporates a double-glazed fire-rated roof access hatch/smoke ventilation actuator above the main stair core, together with roof anchors for maintenance, 30 photovoltaic panels, and two rooflights. Overall, the scheme represents the partial retention of the Sui Generis public house use at lower levels, alongside a significant change of use to residential (Use Class C3) at first floor and above, combined with a substantial upward extension to facilitate additional dwellings.",
